Krita Nova 38 - Photoshop-style committing of text (text tool, part 3)

Krita's text tool already creates point text with a click and a wrapping
text box with a drag, and edits a text clicked on (also on other layers).
What changes, to work like Photoshop's type tool:

- Esc commits the text being edited (deselects it; the tool stays, ready for
  the next text). A drag in progress is still cancelled by Esc.
- Ctrl+Enter, or Enter on the keypad, commits as well.
- Shift+click on a text other than the one being edited starts a new text
  there, instead of editing that text.
- A text that was created but never typed into is removed when editing it
  ends (as an undoable "Remove Empty Text"). Text in a shape keeps its frame.

SvgTextTool: commitText(), removeIfEmpty() (run once the selection change is
over, never while a command is being added), and the key / press handling.
